{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-84237689-79ba-4125-91fa-38575284cb41","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9f0d8aa371fd652","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9013-qlfkk46s/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E001.md","content":"# Cryptographic module audit of the serving stack\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic resolves the central unknown of the FIPS 140-3 compliance strategy:\nwhich serving-stack images link non-validated cryptographic libraries, where\nthose libraries sit relative to the request path, and what remediation each\naffected image requires. Its deliverable — a complete cryptographic module\ninventory plus a per-image remediation plan — is both the scope definition\nfor all downstream remediation work and the module-inventory element of the\ncompliance evidence package required by the strategy.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Enumerate every image in scope: KServe components, the serving data plane,\n  and the Platform Operator image that deploys the stack.\n- For each image, inventory the linked cryptographic libraries and classify\n  each as validated or non-validated against the applicable validated-module\n  program records.\n- Classify each non-validated usage by whether it is in the request path\n  (the strategy only requires validated crypto in the request path).\n- Produce a per-image remediation recommendation (rebuild against validated\n  modules, library replacement, or code change) with estimated effort.\n- Hand the resulting module inventory to the compliance evidence effort as\n  the inventory element of the evidence package.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Every in-scope image has a completed inventory entry listing its linked\n  cryptographic libraries, each classified validated or non-validated with\n  reference to the applicable validated-module records.\n- Every non-validated usage is classified as request-path or non-request-path.\n- Every image with non-validated crypto in the request path has a remediation\n  recommendation with an approach and effort estimate.\n- The inventory and remediation plan are reviewed and accepted by the serving\n  team and the Platform Operator owners.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): produces the module inventory that is a required element of the\n  compliance evidence package.\n- Gates HLR-1 (P0) remediation scope: the audit's outcome determines which\n  images the remediation work must change and how.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":40880,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c7db8851d70b35e","agent_id":"a421b61ecdc3bdc51","session_id":"bb183815-0547-4989-a1f9-5b702edd86b1","uuid":"94dc1e3b-e914-4dfa-b355-c28aa3597f5e","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:52:31.671Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013 into epics"}
