{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-9385f1c9-6bc1-474b-a463-aec9062f8910","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b207533f40e92469","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9013-qlfkk46s/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9013-E003.md","content":"# Platform Operator FIPS validation and remediation\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic covers the Platform Operator's share of HLR-1: the operator image\nthat deploys and reconciles the serving stack must itself be free of\nnon-validated crypto in the request path, and the operator must deploy and\nmanage the stack correctly on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters. It executes\nthe remediation plan for the operator image (if the audit flags one) and\nproduces the operator-side validation evidence for the compliance package.\nIf the cryptographic module audit classifies the operator image as already\nclean, this epic's deliverable reduces to the documented FIPS-cluster\nvalidation of the operator.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Apply the audited remediation approach to the Platform Operator image for\n  any non-validated crypto the audit places in its request path.\n- Rebuild and publish the remediated operator image through the platform\n  build pipeline, retaining the produced build attestations.\n- Verify on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster that the operator deploys and\n  reconciles the serving stack correctly (deployment, upgrade, and status\n  reporting flows).\n- Document the operator's FIPS-cluster validation results (and remediation,\n  if any) and hand them to the compliance evidence effort.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Re-running the audit's detection method against the Platform Operator\n  image shows no non-validated cryptographic library in its request path\n  (either because it was remediated or because the audit classified it\n  clean, with the classification recorded).\n- If remediation was required, the remediated operator image builds green\n  through the platform build pipeline and its build attestations are\n  retained.\n- On a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster, the operator deploys, reconciles, and\n  reports status for the serving stack correctly.\n- The operator-side validation evidence is documented and handed off to the\n  compliance evidence effort.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): all serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters\n  using validated crypto modules (Platform Operator share of HLR-1).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":42895,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c7db8851d70b35e","agent_id":"a421b61ecdc3bdc51","session_id":"bb183815-0547-4989-a1f9-5b702edd86b1","uuid":"11343fe2-7397-45a8-a494-0f216872269f","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:53:02.588Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9013 into epics"}
