{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a46228c6aaadf6de","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n3\ttitle: Cryptographic module audit of the serving stack\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: High\n19\tai_implementability_score: 3\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Cryptographic module audit of the serving stack\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis epic resolves the central unknown of the FIPS 140-3 compliance strategy:\n30\twhich serving-stack images link non-validated cryptographic libraries, where\n31\tthose libraries sit relative to the request path, and what remediation each\n32\taffected image requires. Its deliverable — a complete cryptographic module\n33\tinventory plus a per-image remediation plan — is both the scope definition\n34\tfor all downstream remediation work and the module-inventory element of the\n35\tcompliance evidence package required by the strategy.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Enumerate every image in scope: KServe components, the serving data plane,\n40\t  and the Platform Operator image that deploys the stack.\n41\t- For each image, inventory the linked cryptographic libraries and classify\n42\t  each as validated or non-validated against the applicable validated-module\n43\t  program records.\n44\t- Classify each non-validated usage by whether it is in the request path\n45\t  (the strategy only requires validated crypto in the request path).\n46\t- Produce a per-image remediation recommendation (rebuild against validated\n47\t  modules, library replacement, or code change) with estimated effort.\n48\t- Hand the resulting module inventory to the compliance evidence effort as\n49\t  the inventory element of the evidence package.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- Every in-scope image has a completed inventory entry listing its linked\n54\t  cryptographic libraries, each classified validated or non-validated with\n55\t  reference to the applicable validated-module records.\n56\t- Every non-validated usage is classified as request-path or non-request-path.\n57\t- Every image with non-validated crypto in the request path has a remediation\n58\t  recommendation with an approach and effort estimate.\n59\t- The inventory and remediation plan are reviewed and accepted by the serving\n60\t  team and the Platform Operator owners.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-2 (P0): produces the module inventory that is a required element of the\n65\t  compliance evidence package.\n66\t- Gates HLR-1 (P0) remediation scope: the audit's outcome determines which\n67\t  images the remediation work must change and how.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d8180929c9877b7","agent_id":"a173f98be7b9bcff5","session_id":"bb183815-0547-4989-a1f9-5b702edd86b1","uuid":"0b25f14d-43ee-46bb-9ea0-1e9f339e8c9d","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:55:57.744Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a46228c6aaadf6de","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
