h non-validated crypto in\n51\t  the request path, apply the audited remediation approach (rebuild against\n52\t  validated modules, library replacement, or code change).\n53\t- Rebuild and publish the remediated images through the platform build\n54\t  pipeline, retaining the produced build attestations.\n55\t- Verify serving-stack behavior on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster,\n56\t  covering the deployment modes the serving stack supports.\n57\t- Document the FIPS-cluster test results for each remediated image and hand\n58\t  them, together with the build attestations, to the compliance evidence\n59\t  effort.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- Re-running the audit's detection method against the remediated images\n64\t  shows no non-validated cryptographic library in the request path for any\n65\t  KServe-side serving image.\n66\t- Each remediated image builds green through the platform build pipeline and\n67\t  its build attestations are retained.\n68\t- On a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster, the remediated serving stack deploys\n69\t  and serves inference requests correctly in its supported deployment modes.\n70\t- FIPS-cluster test results and build attestations for every remediated\n71\t  image are documented and handed off to the compliance evidence effort.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- HLR-1 (P0): all serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters\n76\t  using validated crypto modules (KServe and serving data plane share of\n77\t  HLR-1).\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-955bde654b35688a","agent_id":"a9ae5ad5c90ec7192","session_id":"bb183815-0547-4989-a1f9-5b702edd86b1","uuid":"26c407e3-fcad-4d44-8c6f-feb8d21bc80f","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:03:47.490Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf875ffbd5e39e7c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9013 decomposition"}
