perator.\n48\t\n49\t## Scope\n50\t\n51\t- Apply the audited remediation approach to the Platform Operator image for\n52\t  any non-validated crypto the audit places in its request path.\n53\t- Rebuild and publish the remediated operator image through the platform\n54\t  build pipeline, retaining the produced build attestations.\n55\t- Verify on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster that the operator deploys and\n56\t  reconciles the serving stack correctly (deployment, upgrade, and status\n57\t  reporting flows).\n58\t- Document the operator's FIPS-cluster validation results (and remediation,\n59\t  if any) and hand them to the compliance evidence effort.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- Re-running the audit's detection method against the Platform Operator\n64\t  image shows no non-validated cryptographic library in its request path\n65\t  (either because it was remediated or because the audit classified it\n66\t  clean, with the classification recorded).\n67\t- If remediation was required, the remediated operator image builds green\n68\t  through the platform build pipeline and its build attestations are\n69\t  retained.\n70\t- On a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster, the operator deploys, reconciles, and\n71\t  reports status for the serving stack correctly.\n72\t- The operator-side validation evidence is documented and handed off to the\n73\t  compliance evidence effort.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- HLR-1 (P0): all serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters\n78\t  using validated crypto modules (Platform Operator share of HLR-1).\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-955bde654b35688a","agent_id":"a9ae5ad5c90ec7192","session_id":"bb183815-0547-4989-a1f9-5b702edd86b1","uuid":"69468053-f6c8-4aec-b2c1-519ab6e3d106","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:03:48.151Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-abbf8aa0466de21e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-pur