{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88d21c7a7f2ab0a4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E005\n3\ttitle: FIPS compliance evidence package and certification submission\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9013-E002\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9013-E003\n13\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: The package's contents are rewritten to match the audited module\n17\t    inventory and the remediation outcomes; a materially different audit result changes\n18\t    which images require inventory entries, attestations, and test results.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: -1\n24\t  open_questions: 1\n25\t  external_dependency: -1\n26\t  human_process_gates: -1\n27\t  repo_access: 0\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Medium\n32\tai_implementability_score: 0\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# FIPS compliance evidence package and certification submission\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tThis epic delivers HLR-2: the FIPS 140-3 compliance evidence package for the\n41\tmodel serving stack — module inventory, build attestations, and test results\n42\t— assembled and shepherded through the mandatory internal security review\n43\tboard sign-off and submitted to the external accredited certification lab.\n44\tIt consumes the deliverables of the audit and the image remediation work:\n45\ttheir module inventory, build attestations, and FIPS-cluster test results\n46\tare the content of the package, which is why it runs after they complete.\n47\t\n48\t## Scope\n49\t\n50\t- Assemble the evidence package from: the cryptographic module inventory,\n51\t  the build attestations produced by the platform build pipeline for every\n52\t  remediated image, and the FIPS-cluster test results for the serving stack\n53\t  and the Platform Operator.\n54\t- Structure the package to the certification lab's required format for\n55\t  validated-module compliance evidence.\n56\t- Drive the package through the internal security review board sign-off at\n57\t  the milestones the process defines.\n58\t- Submit the signed-off package to the external accredited certification\n59\t  lab and see it triaged/accepted for review.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- The evidence package contains, for every serving-stack image in scope:\n64\t  its module inventory entry, its build attestations (including the signed\n65\t  attestations produced by the platform build pipeline), and its\n66\t  FIPS-cluster test results.\n67\t- The package passes the internal security review board sign-off at the\n68\t  defined milestones.\n69\t- The package is submitted to the external accredited certification lab and\n70\t  triaged for review (submission and triage are the engineering completion\n71\t  point; the lab's certification turnaround is externally controlled and\n72\t  tracked as a risk, not an acceptance criterion).\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- HLR-2 (P0): a compliance evidence package (module inventory, build\n77\t  attestations, test results) is assembled and submitted through the\n78\t  security review board to the external certification lab.\n79\t\n80\t## Risks and Notes\n81\t\n82\t- Certification-lab turnaround is historically six to nine months and the\n83\t  security review board meets on its own cadence; both are externally\n84\t  controlled and cannot be compressed by engineering effort (flagged in the\n85\t  strategy's open questions). Schedule planning must account for this\n86\t  queueing time independently of the engineering work above.\n87\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-to