{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-806f4e97d84e1727","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E002\n3\ttitle: FIPS remediation of KServe serving-stack images\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the audit finds materially more or fewer affected images than\n15\t    estimated, or divergent remediation approaches, the epic's scope is rewritten\n16\t    to match the audited remediation plan (and re-split per image or per runtime if\n17\t    the findings warrant separate review cycles).\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 3\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# FIPS remediation of KServe serving-stack images\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis epic makes the KServe serving-stack images and the serving data plane\n40\tcomply with HLR-1: they must run correctly on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters\n41\tusing validated cryptographic modules, with no non-validated crypto in the\n42\trequest path. It executes the per-image remediation plan produced by the\n43\tcryptographic module audit (on which it depends: the audit's module inventory\n44\tand remediation plan define this epic's concrete scope and approach) and\n45\tgenerates the test results and build attestations that feed the compliance\n46\tevidence package.\n47\t\n48\t## Scope\n49\t\n50\t- For every KServe-side image the audit flagged with non-validated crypto in\n51\t  the request path, apply the audited remediation approach (rebuild against\n52\t  validated modules, library replacement, or code change).\n53\t- Rebuild and publish the remediated images through the platform build\n54\t  pipeline, retaining the produced build attestations.\n55\t- Verify serving-stack behavior on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster,\n56\t  covering the deployment modes the serving stack supports.\n57\t- Document the FIPS-cluster test results for each remediated image and hand\n58\t  them, together with the build attestations, to the compliance evidence\n59\t  effort.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- Re-running the audit's detection method against the remediated images\n64\t  shows no non-validated cryptographic library in the request path for any\n65\t  KServe-side serving image.\n66\t- Each remediated image builds green through the platform build pipeline and\n67\t  its build attestations are retained.\n68\t- On a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster, the remediated serving stack deploys\n69\t  and serves inference requests correctly in its supported deployment modes.\n70\t- FIPS-cluster test results and build attestations for every remediated\n71\t  image are documented and handed off to the compliance evidence effort.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- HLR-1 (P0): all serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters\n76\t  using validated crypto modules (KServe and serving data plane share of\n77\t  HLR-1).\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bacfe8ea362d9293","agent_id":"ac3468000e703d62b","session_id":"bb183815-0547-4989-a1f9-5b702edd86b1","uuid":"8d0bd6e6-5564-464d-84dc-187565c9d3df","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:05:38.418Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-806f4e97d84e1727","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9013 after revision"}
