{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaef53c5ba8c6384","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9013-E003\n3\ttitle: Platform Operator FIPS validation and remediation\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9013\n5\tcomponent: Platform Operator\n6\tteam: RHOAI Platform\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9013-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the audit classifies the Platform Operator image as already\n15\t    clean of non-validated request-path crypto, the epic reduces to documented FIPS-cluster\n16\t    validation only; if it finds more affected surfaces, the remediation scope is\n17\t    rewritten to match the audited plan.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 0\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Medium\n31\tai_implementability_score: 2\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Platform Operator FIPS validation and remediation\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis epic covers the Platform Operator's share of HLR-1: the operator image\n40\tthat deploys and reconciles the serving stack must itself be free of\n41\tnon-validated crypto in the request path, and the operator must deploy and\n42\tmanage the stack correctly on FIPS-enabled OpenShift clusters. It executes\n43\tthe remediation plan for the operator image (if the audit flags one) and\n44\tproduces the operator-side validation evidence for the compliance package.\n45\tIf the cryptographic module audit classifies the operator image as already\n46\tclean, this epic's deliverable reduces to the documented FIPS-cluster\n47\tvalidation of the operator.\n48\t\n49\t## Scope\n50\t\n51\t- Apply the audited remediation approach to the Platform Operator image for\n52\t  any non-validated crypto the audit places in its request path.\n53\t- Rebuild and publish the remediated operator image through the platform\n54\t  build pipeline, retaining the produced build attestations.\n55\t- Verify on a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster that the operator deploys and\n56\t  reconciles the serving stack correctly (deployment, upgrade, and status\n57\t  reporting flows).\n58\t- Document the operator's FIPS-cluster validation results (and remediation,\n59\t  if any) and hand them to the compliance evidence effort.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- Re-running the audit's detection method against the Platform Operator\n64\t  image shows no non-validated cryptographic library in its request path\n65\t  (either because it was remediated or because the audit classified it\n66\t  clean, with the classification recorded).\n67\t- If remediation was required, the remediated operator image builds green\n68\t  through the platform build pipeline and its build attestations are\n69\t  retained.\n70\t- On a FIPS-enabled OpenShift cluster, the operator deploys, reconciles, and\n71\t  reports status for the serving stack correctly.\n72\t- The operator-side validation evidence is documented and handed off to the\n73\t  compliance evidence effort.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- HLR-1 (P0): all serving-stack images run correctly on FIPS-enabled clusters\n78\t  using validated crypto modules (Platform Operator share of HLR-1).\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bacfe8ea362d9293","agent_id":"ac3468000e703d62b","session_id":"bb183815-0547-4989-a1f9-5b702edd86b1","uuid":"1198c2b5-bf46-42bd-88ab-b8d589f08d6f","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:05:39.051Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaef53c5ba8c6384","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-pur