than rebuilding it. No work-product mixing: content\nauthoring is isolated in E006. The E002 size overage is handled exactly\nper the overage carve-out: it is acknowledged in Health Warnings with a\nconcrete, measurable re-split trigger (per image or per serving runtime if\nthe audit finds materially more affected images/libraries or divergent\nremediation approaches), so it is a managed trade-off, not a defect.\n\n### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\nE001 is a genuine Investigation: its outcome (which images link\nnon-validated crypto, and the per-image remediation approach) rewrites the\nscope of E002, determines whether E003 is remediation or validation-only,\nand defines E004's detection criteria — all four dependents exist and cite\nit. E002–E006 are Implementations producing concrete artifacts (rebuilt\nimages with attestations, a gating CI stage, the evidence package,\npublished docs). Every `gated_by` (E002/E003/E004/E005 → E001) has\n`gate_failure_impact` populated with both `action: rewrite` and a\nsubstantive `fallback_approach` describing what actually changes on a\ndifferent audit outcome — true gates, not scheduling dependencies. Every\n`gated_by` target appears in that epic's direct `dependencies` list.\n\n### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\nCorrect rubric per type: E001 carries `investigation_signals` (5-signal);\nE002–E006 carry `ai_signals` (9-signal). All six ai-signals files exist and\ntheir rationale tables match the frontmatter values. E001's signals are\nwell justified (static inspection of published images plus public\nvalidated-module records → source_accessibility 1, local_runnability 1,\nno cluster/human gate). E002's `open_questions: -1` is consistent with its\naudit gate, while E004's `open_questions: 0` is defensible — its design is\nfully determined and only the module-criteria data comes from the audit.\n`architecture_claims` calibration verified against `.context`: the only\narchitecture-context file present is\n`architecture/rhoai-3.0/kserve.md` (which records KServe as Konflux\nonboarded), so E002/E004/E005 scoring 1 with kserve.md citations is\ncorroborated, and E003/E006 scoring 0 due to absent context files for\nPlatform Operator and Documentation is the honest score — the gaps are\nflagged in the Health Warnings rather than papered over.\n\n### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\nEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the strategy. Rule-mandated ACs\nare present where applicable: E006 has the technical-review-before-\npublication AC (docs-authoring); E002 and E003 each have the\n\"builds green through the platform build pipeline with attestations\nretained\" AC (the Rule 25 shape, correctly used instead of DAG edges);\nE002/E003 are remediation passes, not feature replacements, so no\nrollback/feature-flag AC is required. Soft-AC discipline is exemplary:\nthe externally controlled lab turnaround and review-board cadence are\nrecorded in E005's Risks/Notes and the summary's Health Warnings, while\nthe ACs sit at the engineering completion point the strategy controls\n(package assembled, sign-off obtained, submission made and triaged) — the\nreview-board sign-off AC is a verification of the epic's own deliverable\nmandated by HLR-2, not a misfiled availability precondition. No epic body\nreferences sibling epics by draft ID (checked; siblings are referenced by\nname only).\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\nThe full strategy scope is covered: all four HLRs, the serving data plane\n(explicitly in E001's enumeration, E002's scope, and E004's coverage), the\nPlatform Operator image (E003), the security review board path and\nexternal lab submission (E005), and the out-of-scope boundaries (E006's\ncontent explicitly refuses to claim workbenches/pipelines/training/Common\nCriteria). Strategy-level context is carried forward, not dropped: the\nincompressible external gates from the Open Questions section appear in\nE005's Risks and the summary Health Warnings; the missing strategy\nsections (no Impacted Teams, no Dependencies table, no NFRs) are\ndocumented as non-blocking warnings with inferred team assignments flagged\nfor verification. No docs-support prerequisite is stated in the strategy,\nyet the docs epic exists anyway because HLR-4 demands it — Rule 11\nsatisfied.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":33739,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bacfe8ea362d9293","agent_id":"ac3468000e703d62b","session_id":"bb183815-0547-4989-a1f9-5b702edd86b1","uuid":"b800eeba-2613-4757-8432-0d13cee39d9d","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:08:14.603Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9013 after revision"}
